course: dictionary
lesson: 6231
title: Mo: a moment, a moustache, a name
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one you need. «Just a mo, I'm nearly ready» is about waiting, because the words around it talk about being ready. Look at the clues before you choose a meaning.
explain: In British talk, «a mo» is an informal way of saying a moment, a very short time. «Half a mo» means half a moment. Nobody measures it: it can be a few seconds or a little longer, just like «a tick» or «two shakes».
explain: In Australia and New Zealand, «a mo» means a moustache. If the sentence is about a face or a bushy lip, that is the meaning. «Movember» is a November charity month when men grow moustaches.
explain: Mo can also be a name, short for Mohammed, Maureen or Morris. A capital M in a sentence about a person, such as «Mo ran the fastest lap», is often a clue that it is a name. When you are not sure, swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it makes sense.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «A mo» means a moment: a very short time. It is informal, so you would not use it in a formal essay.
fact: In Australia and New Zealand, «a mo» means a moustache, and «Movember» is a charity month when men grow them.
fact: «Mo» can be a short name for Mohammed, Maureen or Morris.
fact: «mo.» is short for month, as in a maths table. «MO» can stand for «modus operandi», a way of doing something, or a medical officer.
exercise: Coach says, «Just a mo, I'm tying my laces.» What does «a mo» mean? | A small dog | A moustache | *A very short moment | A long holiday
exercise: Jack's dad in Perth says, «Look at his mo, it's the best I've seen.» In Australia, what is a mo? | *A moustache | A moment | A river | A short name
exercise: Which of these is a short name for Mohammed, Maureen or Morris? | Month | Movember | *Mo | Moment
test: «Half a mo, I'm nearly finished.» In this sentence, «mo» means: | A name | *A short moment | A moustache | A month
test: In a maths table, «mo.» is short for: | A medal | A moustache | A moment | *A month
exam: In «Mo Salah scored again», what kind of word is Mo? | A month | *A name | A moustache | A moment
